# Installed by framework adoption (2026-09-21). This matters because adoption
# installed `.githooks/pre-push`, a `#!/bin/sh` script: a stale CRLF working
# file is a portability hazard — macOS Git refuses such a hook outright, and
# behavior otherwise varies by platform and shell. `eol=lf`, not bare
# `text=auto`: `text=auto` alone normalises to LF in the repository but still
# checks out CRLF on Windows, which is exactly the case that breaks.
* text=auto eol=lf
